ull, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20284, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_015enr1xu4aTBZUMssfH6b7C", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20284, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01FRFS4Xw6orRfNdVqAmhnCM", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20584, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01FRFS4Xw6orRfNdVqAmhnCM", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20584, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01FRFS4Xw6orRfNdVqAmhnCM", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25830, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0114ux2RMUMazGfB4BasrdCM", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 began failing health checks after deployment to production (error rate ~18% in us-east, us-west and eu-west). v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. I rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt partially failed: an orchestrator error stopped it after us-east, leaving the service on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollout. All regions now run v2.3.0, and the service is healthy with an error rate of ~0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback attempt.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56430, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0114ux2RMUMazGfB4BasrdCM", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56430, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0114ux2RMUMazGfB4BasrdCM", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57994, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_018LxKUhbZECYW8nGDDrnMf3", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58294, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_018LxKUhbZECYW8nGDDrnMf3", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58294, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_018LxKUhbZECYW8nGDDrnMf3", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63233, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, the service is healthy again, and I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks everywhere, with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, had also failed in staging.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. Because it has been healthy before, rolling back to it didn't need change-manager approval.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system. That left us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I retried once and it finished.\n- us-east, us-west and eu-west now all run v2.3.0. Health checks pass and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. It had been created, so I didn't submit it again, and the on-call engineer was paged once.\n- INC-0001 is open as SEV2 for checkout-api. It describes the failed release, the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the current state.\n- It lists two follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed, and why the first rollback attempt stopped partway.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QGhHjcjg5EZsrjZkw9fkTJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GasH3nnQVLuAXkoFeXcPRu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Fdg73a8r1Nz3X2ddfuAB6z", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011LHyApbnBeNcCmd1FYAyTv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Running the same rollback to the same version again is safe, so I'll try it once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013kprjCmtcpKQGYbnNFftAB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015enr1xu4aTBZUMssfH6b7C", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FRFS4Xw6orRfNdVqAmhnCM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0114ux2RMUMazGfB4BasrdCM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 began failing health checks after deployment to production (error rate ~18% in us-east, us-west and eu-west). v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. I rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt partially failed: an orchestrator error stopped it after us-east, leaving the service on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollout. All regions now run v2.3.0, and the service is healthy with an error rate of ~0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback attempt.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_018LxKUhbZECYW8nGDDrnMf3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, the service is healthy again, and I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks everywhere, with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, had also failed in staging.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. Because it has been healthy before, rolling back to it didn't need change-manager approval.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system. That left us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I retried once and it finished.\n- us-east, us-west and eu-west now all run v2.3.0. Health checks pass and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. It had been created, so I didn't submit it again, and the on-call engineer was paged once.\n- INC-0001 is open as SEV2 for checkout-api. It describes the failed release, the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the current state.\n- It lists two follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed, and why the first rollback attempt stopped partway.", "type": "text"}]}]}